//
// Property tests for the round-down-in-vault-favor invariant + redeem
// roundtrip + seed-once. Closes the VAULT-09 property-test supplement
// (per CONTEXT.md "Property test scope").
//
// Three tests:
//   1. compute_shares_to_mint_rounds_down_in_vault_favor_50_random_cases —
//      50 (deposit, total_assets, total_shares) tuples generated by
//      Python random.Random(seed=42). Each case asserts
//      compute_shares_to_mint == floor(deposit * (total_shares +
//      virtual_shares) / (total_assets + 1)). The floor on the right is
//      computed in Python at generation time and inlined as the fourth
//      tuple element. Covers Pitfall 12 (round-down-in-vault-favor).
//
//   2. redeem_request_then_fulfill_returns_at_most_proportional_NAV —
//      W5 LOCK: full request -> warp-clock -> fulfill flow with payout
//      assertion. Asserts actual_payout <= expected_payout (proportional
//      NAV bound) AND actual_payout <= seed + extra_balance (liquidity
//      bound). The placeholder discard form documented in the original
//      plan body is REPLACED by the actual fulfill flow with bounds.
//
//   3. create_vault_seed_transaction_succeeds_once — Sui shared-object
//      semantics make a SECOND create_vault call with the same
//      PendingTreasury impossible: PendingTreasury is consumed by value
//      at first call. Test confirms behaviorally that after share::init
//      + share::consume_pending, the PendingTreasury is no longer in
//      the deployer's inventory.
//
// Note on test 2: production `vault::create_vault` calls
// `predict::create_manager(ctx)` which requires a live Predict shared
// object. Pure-Move tests use `vault::new_vault_for_testing` instead
// (the test-only constructor that bypasses Predict). The seeded state
// is identical: 10 DUSDC quote in balance, 1M virtual shares burned to
// @0xdead. This matches the precedent set by Plan 02-05's
// redeem_test.move and Plan 02-04's supply_test.move.

#[test_only]
